body:
My current setup looks somewhat like this:

```js
var search = instantsearch({
        appId: appId,
        apiKey: apiKey,
        indexName: 'kategorien',
        urlSync: false,
        searchParameters: {
                hierarchicalFacetsRefinements: {
                        facet: ['Fehlbildungen']
                }
        }
});

search.addWidget(
        instantsearch.widgets.searchBox({
                container: '#indikationen_search'
        })
);

search.addWidget(
        instantsearch.widgets.menu({
                container: '#categories',
                attributeName: 'facet',
                sortBy: ['name:asc']
        })
);

search.start();

// reset set filters when typing
$('input#indikationen_search').on('keyup', function(){
        search.helper.clearRefinements();
});
```

By default Algolia hides all categories/facet that have no result when I type something, so the categories expand to full width, which looks odd:

![screen shot 2017-09-12 at 2 27 18 pm](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/3603346/30325840-95b9d0c0-97c6-11e7-9f8a-369cc7627b9d.png)

Standard:

![screen shot 2017-09-12 at 2 27 10 pm](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/3603346/30325850-a688f296-97c6-11e7-8c45-02a694cde858.png)

**Is it possible to have all categories visible but to disable them (when there are no results within a facet/category), so a user cannot click on them? But they should be visible at all times.**
